@@ -283,3 +283,8 @@ Android API 面登记见 `docs/AGENTS/ANDROID-API-USAGE.md` §1/§3/§4/§8；
 `AppFilesDocumentsProvider.kt` registers `${applicationId}.documents` as a system SAF `DocumentsProvider`, with the Android `MANAGE_DOCUMENTS` binding permission and URI grants. The exposed root is **`filesDir` only** (`files/`), not the app's private SharedPreferences/databases/cache or `/data/data` generally. Android's file picker mediates all third-party document grants; files are not globally readable.
 
 `AppDocumentsPath.kt` is the single source of truth for stable `files:` document IDs, canonical containment and symlink/traversal rejection; `AppDocumentsPathTest.kt` tests identity, unsafe names, path escapes and the SAF manifest declaration. Direct edits through the file picker can still change/delete engine data: warn users to back up before changing the runtime, and do not recursively delete directories from the provider. The UI language selector was removed from `GuideManagementController.kt` and the responsive Web UI. `AppLanguage.kt` now forces Korean for Android resources, the engine profile, and the WebView bootstrap, ignoring old stored choices. The existing JS bridge language setter returns Korean for compatibility rather than changing languages.
+
+
+### Korean-only application lifecycle
+
+`KoreanOnlyApplication.kt` is registered on the manifest `<application>` and sets the process default locale to Korean in `attachBaseContext`, `onCreate`, and on configuration changes. Every Android process (including headless engine/overlay services) therefore selects Korean native copy. Legacy Chinese-text JVM contract tests still run without Android Application; their test-only baseline does **not** become a user setting. `AppLanguage` ignores legacy stored choices and forces `ko` into the engine profile and WebView bootstrap.
